  "description": "<p><strong>Highlights</strong><br>\r\n🔪 Walk through the real streets where the Jack the Ripper murders took place<br>\r\n🕵️ Discover the evidence, suspects, and eyewitness accounts behind the mystery<br>\r\n🏙️ Explore the historic district of Whitechapel and its atmospheric alleyways<br>\r\n📜 Learn about Victorian London’s darker history and infamous crime scenes<br>\r\n🍺 End your tour near the legendary Ten Bells Pub, closely linked to the Ripper story<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>General Info</strong><br>\r\n📅 Date &amp; time: choose directly from ticket selector<br>\r\n📍 Location: West Entrance to Altab Ali Park by the large Iron Arch Gate<br>\r\n⏳ Duration: 2 hours<br>\r\n👤 Age: Suitable for adults and older children interested in history and mystery (Child tickets: ages 2–17, Adult tickets: 18+)<br>\r\n❗&nbsp;Please arrive 10–15 minutes before the scheduled start time<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Description</strong><br>\r\nStep into the foggy streets of Victorian London as your expert Ripperologist guide leads you through the real locations where Jack the Ripper stalked his victims in 1888. On this immersive walking tour, you will uncover chilling details, examine evidence, and hear eyewitness accounts surrounding the infamous crimes that shocked London. Explore Whitechapel's historic streets, learn about the darker history of Victorian London, and discover the crime scenes that made this mystery one of the world’s greatest unsolved cases. Get your tickets now!</p>",
